## Context

- **Task 1581 (P5) completed**: SST_PLTS neurodegeneration leading-edge gene extraction
  - 6 leading-edge genes from KEGG "Pathways of neurodegeneration" (padj=0.0147): NOS1, UCHL1, PRNP, GRIA3, CALM2, CHRM3
  - NOT mitochondrial (Complex I-V) or apoptotic (BCL2/caspases) — multi-pathway convergent vulnerability
  - Categories: Calcium/excitotoxicity 3/6 (CALM2, CHRM3, GRIA3), Protein QC 2/6 (UCHL1, PRNP), Nitrosative stress 1/6 (NOS1)
  - **Key finding: FOS→NOS1 double-hit model** — activity-dependent TF directly regulates strongest neurodegeneration gene
  - Created RD task #1674 to evaluate NOS1 as therapeutic target (NOS1 inhibitors exist)
  - Output: sst_plts_neurodegeneration_leading_edge.csv, sst_plts_neurodegeneration_analysis.json

